zkapi (https://github.com/ethereum/zkapi)
  Vendored in vendor/zkapi/ at commit 4ac25c811318d96a873b8b232c7be2252e16c0bd:
  protocol/rust and protocol/setup/v2-concession-dev.
  Licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0 (workspace Cargo.toml). The upstream
  repository root has no license file; a request is open at ethereum/zkapi#28.

  Patches applied after the upstream snapshot. Commits: 1 = 57a0915, 2 = 1e4517b,
  3 = 0bea0cb and 995bf31, 4 = 090ee59, 5 = 117f25f, 6 = 3992a98 (the wallet.rs
  hunk only; the commit also holds nymirad changes), 7 = 7687574.
  1. zkapi PR #22 (head 8a96d2aa0bd983eba1f226e5dff827aab38d88d0):
     zkapi-types/src/felt.rs rejects non-hex characters in Felt252::from_hex.
  2. Poseidon parameters exported as constants from zkapi-core
     (v2.rs: POSEIDON_FULL_ROUNDS, POSEIDON_PARTIAL_ROUNDS, POSEIDON_RATE,
     POSEIDON_CAPACITY, POSEIDON_ALPHA, POSEIDON_SKIP_MATRICES).
  3. Setup patch: CEREMONY_VK_KECCAK256 holds our ceremony's key hashes (the final
     ceremony's); new setup id "nymira" with NYMIRA_VK_KECCAK256 and its own pin
     check (zkapi-proof/src/compact.rs); zkapi-browser accepts both ids
     (bundle_setup_ids); one test for the nymira pin check; the legacy setup/v2
     manifest test skips when that directory is absent.
  4. Manifest only: the vendored workspace's path dependencies (zkapi-types,
     zkapi-core, zkapi-proof, zkapi-client) get version = "0.2.0", so cargo deny
     does not read them as wildcards.
  5. zkapi-core embeds the Poseidon round constants and MDS matrix
     (src/poseidon_params.rs, from examples/gen_poseidon_params.rs; a test
     regenerates them) instead of deriving them on every call, and re-exports
     Felt252 and MERKLE_DEPTH. Same hashes, no circuit change.
  6. Wallet::set_request_time (zkapi-client/src/wallet.rs): the request proof's
     request_time can be set by the caller, so nymirad stamps the operator's signed
     time on a coarse grid. Without a call the wallet stamps the local clock, as upstream
     does. Exit locks, the near-expiry check and ownership proofs are unchanged.
  7. Wallet::set_http_client (zkapi-client/src/wallet.rs, testnet_auth.rs): every
     operator call of the wallet can go through a client the caller supplies (nymirad
     passes a Tor circuit). Without a call the wallet builds its own client, as upstream does.
  8. zkapi-proof/tests/proofs.rs: the release-key check reads request.vk (a verifying key)
     where upstream read request.pk, which only ever reached its refusal branch; with the
     final ceremony's pins the acceptance branch runs and passes.
  Not applied: zkapi PR #29 (sdk/ only; the JS SDK is not vendored).
  No circuit change.

