nearai-inference-sdk 0.1.0 (https://github.com/nearai/inference-sdk)
  Vendored in vendor/nearai-inference-sdk/. Licensed under MIT.
  Patch: every client that fetches evidence can go through a SOCKS5 proxy.
  The upstream clients connect directly. Changes: AttestationClient::with_socks_proxy
  (cloud_api.rs); create_pinned_tls_client_via (pinned_tls.rs); a socks_proxy option on
  InferenceClientOptions and DirectInferenceClientOptions, used for the Gateway
  attestation fetch and the pinned client (inference.rs, direct.rs);
  a client option on DefaultTdxQuoteVerifier and verify_tdx_quote_with_client (quote.rs); reqwest's
  "socks" feature; tests/socks_proxy.rs. Later patches: fetch_model_attestations_with_nonce
  and fetch_gateway_attestation_with_nonce (cloud_api.rs, for replaying recorded reports);
  the sigstore-based image provenance modules (provenance.rs, deployment_provenance.rs) and
  their dependency are removed, which lets the crate join this workspace's lockfile; the
  crate's own Cargo.lock is dropped.

dcap-qvl 0.3.12 (https://github.com/Phala-Network/dcap-qvl)
  Vendored in vendor/dcap-qvl/ (src/ only). Licensed under MIT.
  Patch: get_collateral_with_client takes the HTTP client from the caller, so the
  PCCS fetch can go through a SOCKS5 proxy; get_collateral calls it. Also removed: the Python
  bindings (the `python` feature, pyo3) and reqwest's `hickory-dns` feature, which the client
